# Line endings are decided here rather than by whatever each machine has
# configured. Without this, a checkout on Windows with core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites every file on the way in and warns on the way back out, and the
# same file disagrees with itself between a Windows and a Linux checkout.
#
# LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree. Nothing tracked
# here needs CRLF: the only files that genuinely do are the .cmd shims, and
# those are written at install time rather than stored.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, so Git neither converts them nor tries to diff them as text.
*.png binary
